{
  "key": "gh-1649",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[BUG] main is red: 8 pre-existing test failures (daily_publish elapsed lost, publish_staging stamps) — blocks local pre-commit",
    "description": "Clean-HEAD worktree at fe3ae08996 reproduces 8 pre-existing test failures — unrelated to any new work, they block every local pre-commit run:

- `test/daily_publish_report_signal_test.dart` (2): the cancelled-leg digest lost its elapsed extraction — expects `5h59m53s`, prints `killed after unknown elapsed` (regression from the gh-1600 cancelled-leg digest rework: the watcher-death path no longer carries the job's started/finished timestamps into the section).
- `test/publish_staging_test.dart` (2): `stamp_staged_release.sh` curated-`## <version>` section folding / no-duplicate behavior.
- +4 more across the same two files (full-suite hook run: +10718 passed / −8 failed).

Impact: every local commit fails the pre-commit hook on these 8 regardless of content (one unrelated one-liner had to land via `--no-verify`, PR #1648).

Fix direction: the digest must resolve elapsed from the job's timestamps even on the watcher-killed path (`killed after <elapsed> elapsed`), and the stamp script must satisfy its own spec tests. Keep the tests as the spec — do not weaken them."
  }
}

